AGENTS.md	- Rename brand gate: `sh scripts/check-rename-clean.sh` must pass (residue is an exact baseline diff; runs under Git Bash and `winuxsh -c` alike). Intentional residue change → regenerate `scripts/check-rename-clean.baseline` via `sh scripts/check-rename-clean.sh --regen` and review the diff.
AGENTS.md	- Runtime environment variables use the `NIU_` prefix. During the transition, niubash also sets/reads the deprecated `WINUXSH_SHELL` and `WINUXSH_ROOT` names because current rubash upstream still reads them; these bridges are marked with comments and must be removed once rubash renames its readers. (The `*_SHELL_PATH_STYLE` pair was retired rubash-side in rubash#556 / rubash#537: the engine always renders `$PWD`/`pwd` in the POSIX persona form, and niubash no longer exports the variables.)
AGENTS.md	- Use `~/.niubashrc` as the primary-only interactive user entry point for plugin lists, theme selection, exports, aliases, functions, and shell startup logic. Do not read, migrate, delete, or modify the legacy `~/.winuxshrc` and `~/.winshrc` startup files. An explicitly opted-in `~/.bashrc` fallback is a future plan only, not supported behavior. Startup must not automatically run setup or plugin sync, create the primary rc, or rewrite user rc files. Issue #359 case A (1.4.2): plugin management never writes the rc at all — the manifest (`plugins.toml` + `sources/registry.toml`) drives the generated loader `~/.niubash/generated/plugins.niu`, which the host sources read-only BEFORE the user rc; `niu setup` still writes the rc (create/whole-file) until its 1.4.3 create-only convergence. Never re-attach the retired managed-block writers (`assets::write_managed_block`/`remove_managed_block`) to any verb — the 359.12 structure ratchet fails the build's test suite if you do.
